<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhiban</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dibon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dhiban, biblical Dibon, is a town in Jordan east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dead-sea">Dead Sea</a> and north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnon">Arnon</a> gorge. In the 9th century BCE it was the capital of the kingdom of Moab under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesha">King Mesha</a>, who recorded his building works there. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesha-stele">Mesha Stele</a> was discovered at the site in 1868, and excavations have uncovered remains from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-bronze-age">Early Bronze Age</a> to the Islamic period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dhiban.jpg" alt="Dhiban" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bporter615 at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhiban.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
